    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309">

                <pb facs="0311" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg303"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/906: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Prendergast</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-04-24T14:00:00-04:00">April 24, 1939—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:03 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. In a lengthy official manifesto just published in afternoon press President
                    Busch announces his assumption of complete power in the State and promises a
                    government of “energy and discipline.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Prendergast</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
